      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b46bf3d6-ffc3-424d-bd92-dcc4251a08dc",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students will meet with both expert and jigsaw groups to share findings and begin synthesizing patterns that will become actionable guidance for trusting AI's credibility.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students take out their Milestone 3 Learning Log.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Organize students into their Expert Groups based on the specific exploration they completed in the previous lesson.",
        "name": "Jigsaw Synthesis"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b46bf3d6-ffc3-424d-bd92-dcc4251a08dc",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "00430970-abd8-4d5d-b9ff-834c1b1dc891",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "First, meet with others who did the same exploration as you. You are the experts on that specific task.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "00430970-abd8-4d5d-b9ff-834c1b1dc891",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e8e5e6cf-644a-4500-a8ad-94005aff64cc",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Reform groups with members from different Explorations and Mini-Lessons."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e8e5e6cf-644a-4500-a8ad-94005aff64cc",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b1595cf0-2153-47c8-b663-b7100e9bf135",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Now we will transition into jigsaw group. Share one finding from your Expert Group. As a group, focus on patterns and rules you found rather than just retelling the steps that you went through.",
        "remarks": true,
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Remind students to name specific evidence (an edit, a prompt change, or a missing emotional beat) that shows where human input mattered."
          },
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Listen for students articulating both a tipping point and a human necessity when sharing their examples."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b1595cf0-2153-47c8-b663-b7100e9bf135",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "73f7f6d2-99f4-4fb1-ab57-2f452da6ce4e",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "73f7f6d2-99f4-4fb1-ab57-2f452da6ce4e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c54b27fe-1075-462d-81b9-32a903e649d0",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students synthesize their exploration findings to design a clear, practical Trust Meter that helps others decide when to trust AI and when to slow down and verify.",
        "duration": "20",
        "name": "Project Work"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c54b27fe-1075-462d-81b9-32a903e649d0",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "199c7c27-2538-4811-b934-a178fe1bea50",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Use what you discovered in your Explorations, Mini-Lessons, and jigsaw conversations to design a Trust Meter for your AI Responsibility Guide. Your meter should show different levels of trust and clearly explain what moves an AI response up or down. Be specific — include evidence from your testing to justify why something belongs at each level.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "199c7c27-2538-4811-b934-a178fe1bea50",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "501e9184-89a5-424a-9c4a-80c56111c6f6",
      "position": 12,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Students create and add a Trust Meter visual to their project.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Push students beyond vague language like \"check it\" or \"don't trust everything.\" Ask:\n\n- What specifically should someone look for?\n- What detail made you lower your trust during testing?\n- What pattern kept showing up?\n- Encourage conditional thinking instead of absolute rules.\n"
          },
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Look for a Trust Meter that clearly defines multiple levels of trust, includes at least two specific user actions, and references concrete evidence from the student’s exploration to justify their guidance."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "501e9184-89a5-424a-9c4a-80c56111c6f6",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "8d692aea-9a8f-47c3-a6a1-93756c10ddb1",
      "position": 13,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "8d692aea-9a8f-47c3-a6a1-93756c10ddb1",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "1d1dbe4f-549d-45e7-b1b3-e3b07c27787f",
      "position": 14,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 6, Level 1. Students will add to the project they started in Lesson 3.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Push students past vague advice (\"just check it\") by asking what specifically someone should look for, what detail lowered their trust during testing, and what patterns kept showing up encourage conditional thinking instead of absolute rules.",
        "progression_name": "OLD_Project Work - Milestone 3 "
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "1d1dbe4f-549d-45e7-b1b3-e3b07c27787f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "333f09c6-dc03-4728-b75f-1fe6e9a2a41e",
      "position": 15,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "OLD_Project Work - Image Generation",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Students will access to the same Sketch Lab level on which they have been working on throughout the unit. There is also an optional AI Chat level for students to use to generate images for use in their project as needed."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "333f09c6-dc03-4728-b75f-1fe6e9a2a41e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "56feea60-c504-47c0-a4db-09aa1c6cae7b",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click through the animated slide to display the prompts.\n- *If AI is trained on lots of examples, what happens if most of those examples come from the same type of person?*\n- *What happens if certain groups, ideas, or experiences show up less in the data?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students recognize that AI outputs reflect the data they were trained on, and that when that data is unrepresentative, the result is a system with built-in bias that can misrepresent or exclude certain groups and perspectives."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "56feea60-c504-47c0-a4db-09aa1c6cae7b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "b935594c-6d1b-4b2e-a1b8-4629d26245bb"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "17a48065-19c4-4a46-80ac-67b51000c132",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students explore how small pieces of public data can be combined to reveal sensitive information through a high-stakes scenario."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "17a48065-19c4-4a46-80ac-67b51000c132",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1eda96bf-6153-42fc-8db4-009cde952d2b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b358988a-840a-4760-9ec0-2f257faacca7",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Imagine your favorite streamer suddenly stops broadcasting because someone showed up at their house. No one knew where they lived, but they posted one photo. How could that one photo lead someone straight to their door? Today we're starting with a mystery. A famous streamer named Z-Tech went dark because someone found their house using nothing but a selfie. We're going to see if we can figure out how that happened.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b358988a-840a-4760-9ec0-2f257faacca7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1eda96bf-6153-42fc-8db4-009cde952d2b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "bf81aaad-d903-4712-b8c2-c75ad9a37c68",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** With a partner, students examine the selfie to find three specific details in the background that could be used to pinpoint Z-Tech's location.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students who are looking past the person in the photo and at the background. Ask: \"What does that bus number tell you about the school district?\" or \"How many stores in this city carry that specific soda flavor?\"",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Consider zooming in on a few different areas of the sample selfie image so that students can see more detail."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "bf81aaad-d903-4712-b8c2-c75ad9a37c68",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1eda96bf-6153-42fc-8db4-009cde952d2b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "cd8ee64d-a89c-4109-88eb-0fe1b75e5e68",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What could you determine from what you saw in the image?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should realize that small, seemingly \"public\" details (weather, a soda brand) can be combined by a motivated person—or an AI—to reveal \"private\" or \"sensitive\" information like a home address.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Listen for students using the word \"inference\" or describing how one piece of data connects to another."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "cd8ee64d-a89c-4109-88eb-0fe1b75e5e68",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1eda96bf-6153-42fc-8db4-009cde952d2b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "5bc32a27-8afc-449c-98da-0f0515ee80d7",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "5bc32a27-8afc-449c-98da-0f0515ee80d7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1eda96bf-6153-42fc-8db4-009cde952d2b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "905f684a-e552-4518-9685-0cf9fb1e3444",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
