    {
      "key": "aace2c2f-3e46-4f7f-a948-70dbc302eaea",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students select an exploration to uncover both the benefits of sharing data with AI and the hidden risks of data oversharing.",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Explorations",
        "progression_name": "Mini-Lesson: Truth & Credibility with AI"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "aace2c2f-3e46-4f7f-a948-70dbc302eaea",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "149fbba4-dfb1-4b04-931e-1e68c1599d8c",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Verifying AI"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "149fbba4-dfb1-4b04-931e-1e68c1599d8c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "0c104923-f26d-4a38-91f0-5168497922ca",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Project Work"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "0c104923-f26d-4a38-91f0-5168497922ca",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "72abc4e6-166e-46f6-8be2-4a02c9ad3a1d",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Tips for Verifying AI"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "72abc4e6-166e-46f6-8be2-4a02c9ad3a1d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "53ea95bb-7983-4a24-af3e-4f04ef302e25",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Now that we've seen how a single photo can reveal a location, let's look at the different types of data we generate every day.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "53ea95bb-7983-4a24-af3e-4f04ef302e25",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "8e7439e1-e00b-4173-996c-c95087981687",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define *public data*.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define *private data*.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define *sensitive data*.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the explorations by reading the inquiry question.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Transition: Direct students to Lesson 7, Level 1. Students work with a partner at their station to complete a data classification activity in which they are asked to analyze different types of data, with differing contexts, and to sort it into public, private, and sensitive categories.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students who are choosing different explorations. Ask: \"Why did you pick this specific topic?\" Have students justify their inclusion of certain pieces of data into the various categories."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "8e7439e1-e00b-4173-996c-c95087981687",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "7bc91ed3-beda-4902-aabd-9182c45b5775",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "OLD_Safety and Privacy",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Students should test in a rapid and iterative manner throughout this part of the exploration. The intent is for students to have multiple touches and to begin building evidence to support their assertions on how they might best co-create with AI."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "7bc91ed3-beda-4902-aabd-9182c45b5775",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ae6548e8-7562-435d-b736-ab4ad9e3bf2d",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ae6548e8-7562-435d-b736-ab4ad9e3bf2d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ecf8bf9d-0cfe-40d0-a75c-d0b53993443b",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What patterns did you recognize that separate public, private, and sensitive data?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students can quickly share some ways that they classified data and how they chose to differentiate. Some sample patterns that they might identify include:\n- Public data: General preferences, fandoms, or regional pride that help you connect with others but don't put your safety at risk.  (gaming handle, social media likes, t-shirt style)\n- Private data: Information that is unique to you but doesn't necessarily reveal your location. It’s often used for security questions or official records (legal name, birth year, allergies)\n- Sensitive data: Data that reveals exactly where you are, where you live, or your daily routine (house number, wi-fi name)\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 7, Level 2. Students test the AI Chat by providing the AI with different combinations of Public and Private Data and exploring the outputs in terms of privacy and safety.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Ask students what combinations of data that they are providing to the AI and to explain the different results that they have received.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *How much data did the AI need to feel \"personal\" and to provide good output?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Answers will vary; however, students should realize that while more data leads to better personalization, it also increases the risk of revealing sensitive patterns.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 7, Level 3. Students will practice the strategy of anonymizing data and making judgments about the line between safety and security and good AI output.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Assist students with using Sketch Lab as needed. Ask questions about why they anonymized certain details, but did not change others.",
        "progression_name": "OLD_Safety and Privacy"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ecf8bf9d-0cfe-40d0-a75c-d0b53993443b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "db3f05f2-5e1d-4fd3-bf7a-d33842bc01c6",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 7, Level 4. Students select between a mini-lesson to explore a topic of their choice.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Ask students what surprised them.",
        "duration": "10",
        "name": "Mini-Lessons",
        "progression_name": "OLD_Mini-Lessons: Safety and Privacy",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "If students finish early, encourage them to explore a second topic to add context and depth to their project."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "db3f05f2-5e1d-4fd3-bf7a-d33842bc01c6",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
