    {
      "key": "037b5225-cc94-4cde-931c-9cfb05e38bbf",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students will meet with both expert and jigsaw groups to share findings and begin synthesizing patterns that will become actionable guidance for co-creating with AI.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students take out their Milestone 4 Learning Log and their KWL Chart.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Organize students into their Expert Groups based on the specific exploration they completed in the previous lesson.",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Jigsaw Synthesis"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "037b5225-cc94-4cde-931c-9cfb05e38bbf",
        "lesson_activity.key": "d68f3932-1b69-4d73-80c4-078703c1e7c5"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c80d72b4-55bb-4029-a149-37e2dac6a0c9",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "First, meet with your Expert Group to solidify what you learned. You're looking for common threads across your group's findings.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c80d72b4-55bb-4029-a149-37e2dac6a0c9",
        "lesson_activity.key": "d68f3932-1b69-4d73-80c4-078703c1e7c5"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "7d945809-fb11-4dfa-9a8a-68cd8f61e930",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students reflect on their experiences with the previous exploration and consider one of the following questions:\n- What are some common patterns you noticed?\n- What are some risks?\n- What insights and strategies can you share?\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Help students reorganize so each group has a representative from all three explorations. Explain expectations for sharing and note-taking using the Safety and Security Debrief organizer."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "7d945809-fb11-4dfa-9a8a-68cd8f61e930",
        "lesson_activity.key": "d68f3932-1b69-4d73-80c4-078703c1e7c5"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "4a60a85e-6a18-416a-98b7-d837f281b771",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Now, mix it up! In your new Jigsaw Groups, you are the teacher for your exploration. Don't just tell them what you did; tell them what you discovered about how AI uses our information. Look for patterns that appear in all three investigations rather than just retelling the steps that you went through.",
        "remarks": true,
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "If groups are uneven, pair up two students from the same exploration to present together."
          },
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Listen for students articulating evidence that they collected and actionable guidance that results from it."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "4a60a85e-6a18-416a-98b7-d837f281b771",
        "lesson_activity.key": "d68f3932-1b69-4d73-80c4-078703c1e7c5"
      }
    },
